+++
+++<h1>PRD: Messaging Offline Availability — Content Cards, CBE &amp; Inbox (iOS SDK)</h1>
+++
+++<h2>1. Executive summary</h2>
+++<h3>Problem</h3>
+++<p>Content Cards, Code-Based Experiences (CBE), and Inbox feeds today live <strong>primarily in memory</strong>. After app restart or offline use, surfaces are empty until the next successful network fetch. In-App Messages already persist to device and reload on cold start. Customers (e.g. Disney — poor park Wi‑Fi) need messaging content from the <strong>last good online session</strong> available offline.</p>
+++
+++<h3>Proposed solution</h3>
+++<p>Persist eligible proposition rules to device after every <strong>successful</strong> <code>updatePropositionsForSurfaces</code>. On read, the SDK uses a <strong>memory-first, disk-second</strong> strategy — no integrator flag required. Whether a proposition is eligible for disk persistence is controlled by an <strong>authoring-side offline availability flag</strong> delivered in the Edge payload (<code>scopeDetails.characteristics.mobileParameters.offline</code>), with UI placement TBD (see §5.5).</p>
+++
+++<h3>Scope expansion (2026-07-14)</h3>
+++<table class="wrapped"><tbody>
+++<tr><th>Surface type</th><th>Schemas</th><th>Offline persistence</th><th>Read APIs</th></tr>
+++<tr><td><strong>Content Cards</strong></td><td><code>.feed</code>, <code>.contentCard</code></td><td>Proposed ✅ (gated by <code>offlineAvailable</code>)</td><td><code>getPropositionsForSurfaces</code>, <code>getContentCardsUI</code></td></tr>
+++<tr><td><strong>Code-Based Experiences</strong></td><td><code>.jsonContent</code>, <code>.htmlContent</code>, <code>.defaultContent</code></td><td>Proposed ✅ (gated by <code>offlineAvailable</code>)</td><td><code>getPropositionsForSurfaces</code></td></tr>
+++<tr><td><strong>Inbox</strong></td><td><code>.inbox</code> container-item + linked CC propositions</td><td>Proposed ✅ (container + cards; see callouts)</td><td><code>getInboxUI</code> → internal get/update</td></tr>
+++<tr><td><strong>In-App Messages</strong></td><td>IAM rulesets</td><td>Existing (unchanged)</td><td>Automatic on launch</td></tr>
+++</tbody></table>
+++
+++<h3>Key decisions</h3>
+++<ul>
+++<li><strong>No integrator read flag</strong> — SDK auto-hydrates from disk when in-memory data is missing or empty for requested surfaces.</li>
+++<li><strong>Memory-first read order</strong> — always consult session memory before disk.</li>
+++<li><strong>Separate disk keys per surface family</strong> — <code>contentCardPropositions</code>, <code>codeBasedPropositions</code>, <code>inboxPropositions</code> (IAM remains <code>propositions</code>).</li>
+++<li><strong>Save rules, not UI</strong> — store Adobe rules; re-run qualification on read so dismiss/expiry still apply.</li>
+++<li><strong>Authoring gate</strong> — SDK only persists propositions where server sets <code>offlineAvailable: true</code> (defaults <code>true</code> when absent for backward compatibility).</li>
+++<li><strong>Failed fetch protection</strong> — offline/timeout stream close must not mutate any persisted store.</li>
+++<li><strong>Clear on logout</strong> — <code>resetIdentities</code> wipes CC/CBE/Inbox memory + disk (<a href="https://jira.corp.adobe.com/browse/PLATIR-62504">PLATIR-62504</a>).</li>
+++</ul>
+++
+++<h3>Top risks</h3>
+++<ul>
+++<li>Authoring flag placement undecided → payload contract may shift.</li>
+++<li>Offline read latency up to <strong>5 seconds</strong> in current design when reads are queued behind network updates (see Callout §6.1).</li>
+++<li>Inbox requires <strong>both</strong> container-item and card propositions — partial persistence shows error UI.</li>
+++<li>Images may not render offline (lazy cache — <a href="https://jira.corp.adobe.com/browse/PLATIR-44800">PLATIR-44800</a>).</li>
+++<li>Dismissed cards may briefly reappear on cold start until event history catches up (Option B disk eviction open).</li>
+++</ul>
+++
+++<h2>2. Context and problem statement</h2>
+++<h3>2.1 Current behavior (as-is)</h3>
+++<table class="wrapped"><tbody>
+++<tr><th>Action</th><th>Content Cards / CBE / Inbox today</th></tr>
+++<tr><td>Successful online update</td><td>Propositions in memory for this session</td></tr>
+++<tr><td>App killed / cold start</td><td>Memory gone → empty until network</td></tr>
+++<tr><td>Offline</td><td>Empty (unless same-session memory)</td></tr>
+++<tr><td>Logout</td><td>CC cache not cleared → cross-user risk (<a href="https://jira.corp.adobe.com/browse/PLATIR-62504">PLATIR-62504</a>)</td></tr>
+++</tbody></table>
+++
+++<h3>2.2 Customer use case — Disney</h3>
+++<p>In the park, network is often poor. The app needs cards and inbox content available offline and interactive. When online, only deltas should go over the wire. Multiple business units compete for bandwidth — messaging surfaces should not require a fresh fetch on every screen open.</p>
+++
+++<h3>2.3 PLATIR drivers</h3>
+++<table class="wrapped"><tbody>
+++<tr><th>Ticket</th><th>Problem</th><th>Required response</th></tr>
+++<tr><td><a href="https://jira.corp.adobe.com/browse/PLATIR-62504">PLATIR-62504</a></td><td>Cross-user card leakage on shared devices</td><td>Clear CC/CBE/Inbox cache on <code>resetIdentities</code></td></tr>
+++<tr><td><a href="https://jira.corp.adobe.com/browse/PLATIR-54423">PLATIR-54423</a></td><td>Stale cache when server stops sending a feed</td><td>Remove feeds requested but not returned on successful update</td></tr>
+++<tr><td><a href="https://jira.corp.adobe.com/browse/PLATIR-44800">PLATIR-44800</a></td><td>Offline broken images (IAM)</td><td>CC/CBE images lazy — open for product</td></tr>
+++<tr><td><a href="https://jira.corp.adobe.com/browse/PLATIR-64717">PLATIR-64717</a></td><td>Empty <code>items[]</code> proposition shells</td><td>Do not persist empty shells (open)</td></tr>
+++</tbody></table>
+++
+++<h2>3. Goals and non-goals</h2>
+++<h3>3.1 Goals</h3>
+++<ul>
+++<li>G1 — Persist eligible proposition rules after successful online fetch (CC, CBE, Inbox).</li>
+++<li>G2 — SDK reads saved content offline via automatic memory-first + disk hydrate (no app flag).</li>
+++<li>G3 — Authoring controls per-proposition offline eligibility via server payload.</li>
+++<li>G4 — No cross-user leakage on shared devices after logout.</li>
+++<li>G5 — Evict stale feeds when server returns nothing for a requested surface (successful update only).</li>
+++<li>G6 — Same read semantics across <code>getPropositionsForSurfaces</code>, <code>getContentCardsUI</code>, and <code>getInboxUI</code> internal reads.</li>
+++</ul>
+++
+++<h3>3.2 Non-goals (this PRD)</h3>
+++<ul>
+++<li>Android / React Native wrapper exposure (follows iOS).</li>
+++<li>Proactive image/asset prefetch for offline (<a href="https://jira.corp.adobe.com/browse/PLATIR-44800">PLATIR-44800</a>).</li>
+++<li>Public <code>clearCachedContentCardPropositions()</code> API (backlog).</li>
+++<li>Detailed engineering file-level implementation (see repo <code>docs/agents/</code>).</li>
+++</ul>
+++
+++<h2>4. Requirements</h2>
+++<h3>4.1 Functional requirements</h3>
+++<table class="wrapped"><tbody>
+++<tr><th>ID</th><th>Requirement</th></tr>
+++<tr><td>FR-1</td><td>On successful <code>updatePropositionsForSurfaces</code>, persist eligible rules to separate disk keys per surface family</td></tr>
+++<tr><td>FR-2</td><td>On failed/timeout update (zero <code>personalization:decisions</code>), do <strong>not</strong> change phone cache</td></tr>
+++<tr><td>FR-3</td><td><code>getPropositionsForSurfaces</code> returns in-memory data when present; otherwise hydrates from disk automatically</td></tr>
+++<tr><td>FR-4</td><td><code>getContentCardsUI</code> uses same read path as get propositions (no separate flag)</td></tr>
+++<tr><td>FR-5</td><td><code>getInboxUI</code> benefits from same persistence model for inbox surface (container-item + linked cards)</td></tr>
+++<tr><td>FR-6</td><td>SDK persist gate: only propositions with <code>offlineAvailable == true</code> written to disk</td></tr>
+++<tr><td>FR-7</td><td>Requested surface absent from successful server response → remove that surface from relevant disk key</td></tr>
+++<tr><td>FR-8</td><td>Surfaces not part of current update request → leave disk cache unchanged</td></tr>
+++<tr><td>FR-9</td><td><code>resetIdentities</code> clears CC/CBE/Inbox memory + disk; IAM disk unchanged</td></tr>
+++</tbody></table>
+++
+++<h3>4.2 Non-functional requirements</h3>
+++<table class="wrapped"><tbody>
+++<tr><th>ID</th><th>Requirement</th></tr>
+++<tr><td>NFR-1</td><td><strong>Backward compatibility</strong> — payloads without <code>offline</code> flag default to persist (<code>true</code>)</td></tr>
+++<tr><td>NFR-2</td><td><strong>Identity safety</strong> — no prior user's content after logout/login</td></tr>
+++<tr><td>NFR-3</td><td><strong>Read latency</strong> — disk hydrate should complete in &lt;200ms when not blocked by queue (target; see callouts)</td></tr>
+++<tr><td>NFR-4</td><td><strong>Observability</strong> — consider Assurance event when content served from disk (open)</td></tr>
+++</tbody></table>
+++
+++<h2>5. Solution design</h2>
+++
+++<h3>5.1 High-level architecture</h3>
+++<p>End-to-end flow from authoring → server → SDK gates → app APIs.</p>
+++
+++<ac:structured-macro ac:name="code" ac:schema-version="1" ac:macro-id="arch-flow-001"><ac:parameter ac:name="language">text</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">Server → SDK → App (proposed)</ac:parameter><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[
+++┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+++│  AJO AUTHORING (placement TBD — see §5.5)                                   │
+++│  Sets "Offline availability" → serialized into Edge proposition payload    │
+++└──────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────┘
+++                                   │ personalization:decisions (Edge stream)
+++                                   ▼
+++┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+++│  SERVER PAYLOAD                                                              │
+++│  Proposition.scopeDetails.characteristics.mobileParameters.offline: Bool     │
+++│  (defaults true when absent)                                                 │
+++└──────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────┘
+++                                   │
+++          ┌────────────────────────┴────────────────────────┐
+++          │ WRITE PATH (online)                            │ READ PATH (anytime)
+++          ▼                                                ▼
+++┌──────────────────────────┐              ┌──────────────────────────────────┐
+++│ updatePropositions       │              │ getPropositionsForSurfaces       │
+++│ ForSurfaces              │              │ getContentCardsUI                │
+++│                          │              │ getInboxUI (internal get)        │
+++│ 1. Edge stream           │              │                                  │
+++│ 2. Success guard         │              │ 1. Check IN-MEMORY cache  ◄──────┼── FIRST
+++│    (≥1 decisions event)  │              │ 2. If nil/empty → DISK hydrate │
+++│ 3. ParsedPropositions    │              │ 3. Run rules engine            │
+++│    schema routing:       │              │ 4. Return propositions / UI    │
+++│    • CC  → cc key        │              └──────────────────────────────────┘
+++│    • CBE → cbe key       │
+++│    • Inbox → inbox key   │
+++│ 4. SDK GATE:             │
+++│    if offlineAvailable   │
+++│    → write disk          │
+++│ 5. Update memory         │
+++└──────────────────────────┘
+++]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
