+++<h3>5.2 AJO Inbox surface model</h3>
+++<ac:structured-macro ac:name="info" ac:schema-version="1" ac:macro-id="inbox-model-001"><ac:rich-text-body>
+++<p><strong>Important:</strong> AJO authors assign cards a primary surface (<code>s1</code>, <code>s2</code>) and an inbox surface (<code>i1</code>) via <code>inboxSurfaces</code>. IDS remaps the response scope to <code>i1</code>. The SDK <strong>only sees <code>i1</code></strong>.</p>
+++<p>A single <code>updatePropositionsForSurfaces([i1])</code> returns the inbox container-item <strong>and</strong> all linked content cards, all scoped to <code>i1</code>. No separate surface requests needed.</p>
+++</ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
+++
+++<h3>5.3 Data storage (logical)</h3>
+++<ac:structured-macro ac:name="code" ac:schema-version="1" ac:macro-id="storage-001"><ac:parameter ac:name="language">text</ac:parameter><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[Cache file:  com.adobe.messaging.cache
+++
+++Keys (separate, never shared):
+++  propositions              → In-App Messages (existing)
+++  contentCardPropositions   → Content Cards / feeds
+++  codeBasedPropositions     → CBE (json/html/default content)
+++  inboxPropositions         → Inbox container-item schema
+++
+++Format:  JSON { "surfaceUri": [ Proposition, ... ] }
+++What we save: Adobe RULES — not final UI models]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
+++
+++<h3>5.4 API contract &amp; integration patterns</h3>
+++
+++<h4>updatePropositionsForSurfaces — network write</h4>
+++<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Fetch fresh propositions from Edge; on success, update memory and persist eligible rules to disk.</p>
+++<ac:structured-macro ac:name="code" ac:schema-version="1" ac:macro-id="api-update-001"><ac:parameter ac:name="language">swift</ac:parameter><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[Messaging.updatePropositionsForSurfacesWithCompletionHandler([surface]) { success in
+++    // success == true  → stream completed AND ≥1 personalization:decisions received
+++    // success == false → timeout, invalid surfaces, or zero decisions (disk UNCHANGED)
+++}]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
+++
+++<h4>getPropositionsForSurfaces — memory-first read</h4>
+++<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Host apps rendering custom UI (CBE JSON/HTML, custom card feeds, diagnostics).</p>
+++<ac:structured-macro ac:name="code" ac:schema-version="1" ac:macro-id="api-get-001"><ac:parameter ac:name="language">swift</ac:parameter><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[Messaging.getPropositionsForSurfaces([surface]) { propositionsBySurface, error in
+++    // 1. Returns in-memory qualified propositions when available
+++    // 2. Auto-hydrates from disk when memory is nil/empty for requested surface
+++    // 3. Empty result → [] with error == nil
+++}]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
+++
+++<h4>getContentCardsUI — templated card UI</h4>
+++<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Apps using Adobe Content Card UI components. Internally calls <code>getPropositionsForSurfaces</code> — same memory-first + disk hydrate semantics.</p>
+++<ac:structured-macro ac:name="code" ac:schema-version="1" ac:macro-id="api-ccui-001"><ac:parameter ac:name="language">swift</ac:parameter><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[Messaging.getContentCardsUI(for: surface,
+++                              customizer: customizer,
+++                              listener: listener) { result in
+++    // Builds ContentCardUI models from propositions returned by get path
+++}]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
+++
+++<h4>getInboxUI — inbox container + cards</h4>
+++<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Adobe Inbox UI. Requires <strong>both</strong> inbox container-item proposition and content card propositions for the same inbox surface.</p>
+++<ac:structured-macro ac:name="warning" ac:schema-version="1" ac:macro-id="inbox-dep-001"><ac:rich-text-body>
+++<p>If only cards are cached but the inbox container-item is missing, <code>InboxUI</code> shows an error state — even when card data exists on disk. Both must persist for offline inbox.</p>
+++</ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
+++<ac:structured-macro ac:name="code" ac:schema-version="1" ac:macro-id="api-inbox-001"><ac:parameter ac:name="language">swift</ac:parameter><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[Messaging.getInboxUI(for: inboxSurface, ...) { result in
+++    // Internally: updatePropositions → getPropositions
+++    // Once disk hydration is active, offline get can still succeed if both
+++    // container-item and cards were previously persisted
+++}]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
+++
+++<h4>Recommended integration pattern (cache-first)</h4>
+++<ac:structured-macro ac:name="code" ac:schema-version="1" ac:macro-id="pattern-001"><ac:parameter ac:name="language">swift</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">Show cached content immediately; refresh in background</ac:parameter><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[// 1. Read local first (memory → disk auto-hydrate)
+++Messaging.getContentCardsUI(for: surface) { result in
+++    showCards(result)  // instant when cache exists
+++}
+++
+++// 2. Background network refresh (do not block step 1)
+++Messaging.updatePropositionsForSurfacesWithCompletionHandler([surface]) { success in
+++    if success {
+++        Messaging.getContentCardsUI(for: surface) { result in showCards(result) }
+++    }
+++}]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
