++@@ -0,0 +1,130 @@
+++<h3>6.6 Assurance — when and where to add events (OQ-5)</h3>
+++<p><strong>Goal:</strong> During an Adobe Assurance session, integrators and QA can see that content was served from disk (not Edge), why a network call was skipped, and which surface was hydrated.</p>
+++<p><strong>Note:</strong> Disk hydrate itself is fast (&lt;200ms). Assurance should fire at the <strong>decision point</strong>, not on every card render.</p>
+++
+++<h4>Option A — At disk hydrate completion (recommended primary)</h4>
+++<p><strong>Where:</strong> <code>hydrateContentCardRulesEngineFromDisk(for:)</code> — after rules are loaded and the qualified list is built.</p>
+++<p><strong>Assurance event payload:</strong></p>
+++<ac:structured-macro ac:name="code" ac:schema-version="1"><ac:parameter ac:name="language">text</ac:parameter><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[Event name: "Content Cards — hydrated from disk"
+++Fields: surface URI, proposition count, disk key, hydrate duration ms, offlineAvailable flags]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
+++<p><strong>Pros:</strong> Exact moment cache was used; maps 1:1 to SDK behavior.<br/><strong>Cons:</strong> Does not explain <em>why</em> hydrate happened (memory miss vs forced offline path).</p>
+++
+++<h4>Option B — At get/read API response (memory vs disk delta)</h4>
+++<p><strong>Where:</strong> <code>retrieveMessages</code> / <code>getPropositionsForSurfaces</code> completion — compare:</p>
+++<ul>
+++<li>memory had propositions → <strong>source: memory</strong></li>
+++<li>memory empty, disk hydrate ran → <strong>source: disk</strong></li>
+++<li>both empty → <strong>source: none</strong></li>
+++</ul>
+++<p><strong>Pros:</strong> Matches what the app actually received; easy for QA (&quot;did Log Props hit disk?&quot;).<br/><strong>Cons:</strong> Slightly later than hydrate; need to thread <code>propositionSource</code> through the response path.</p>
+++
+++<h4>Option C — At network availability gate (skip Edge)</h4>
+++<p><strong>Where:</strong> <code>updatePropositionsForSurfaces</code> when <code>MobileCore.isNetworkAvailable() == false</code> (or health check fails).</p>
+++<ac:structured-macro ac:name="code" ac:schema-version="1"><ac:parameter ac:name="language">text</ac:parameter><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[Event name: "Content Cards — update skipped (offline)"
+++Fields: surfaces requested, path monitor status, health check result]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
+++<p><strong>Pros:</strong> Explains why no Edge <code>personalization:decisions</code> event appears in Assurance.<br/><strong>Cons:</strong> Does not prove disk content was <em>served</em> — only that network was skipped.</p>
+++
+++<h4>Option D — Combined &quot;proposition source&quot; on every read (A + B)</h4>
+++<p>Emit one Assurance event per <code>getPropositions</code> / <code>getContentCardsUI</code> with:</p>
+++<table class="wrapped"><tbody>
+++<tr><th>Field</th><th>Values</th></tr>
+++<tr><td><code>propositionSource</code></td><td><code>memory</code> | <code>disk</code> | <code>network</code> | <code>none</code></td></tr>
+++<tr><td><code>networkStatus</code></td><td><code>available</code> | <code>unavailable</code> | <code>degraded</code></td></tr>
+++<tr><td><code>surfaces</code></td><td>requested URIs</td></tr>
+++<tr><td><code>latencyMs</code></td><td>end-to-end callback time</td></tr>
+++</tbody></table>
+++<p><strong>Pros:</strong> Single event answers &quot;where did cards come from?&quot; — best for PM/QA demos.<br/><strong>Cons:</strong> More implementation work; needs consistent enum across CC/CBE/Inbox.</p>
+++
+++<ac:structured-macro ac:name="info" ac:schema-version="1" ac:macro-id="assurance-rec-001"><ac:rich-text-body><p><strong>Recommendation (v1):</strong> Ship <strong>Option D</strong> (combined read-path event) + <strong>Option C</strong> (network skip on update). Follow Live Activity pattern: <code>EventSource.debug</code> + named events visible in Assurance Events tab.</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
+++
+++<h3>6.7 Analytics — when and where to add events (OQ-5)</h3>
+++<p><strong>Important distinction:</strong> <code>display</code>, <code>dismiss</code>, and <code>interact</code> are <strong>campaign engagement events</strong> (Edge XDM → AJO reporting). They answer &quot;did the user see/click/dismiss this card?&quot; — not &quot;did the SDK serve it from disk?&quot;</p>
+++<p>Mixing cache source into display/dismiss/interact <strong>pollutes campaign metrics</strong> unless Product explicitly wants that.</p>
+++
+++<h4>Option 1 — Separate SDK operational event (recommended)</h4>
+++<p><strong>Where:</strong> Same as Assurance Option B/D — on successful disk hydrate or disk-served <code>getPropositions</code>.</p>
+++<p><strong>Event type:</strong> New internal/Edge event, e.g. <code>proposition.cache.served</code> — <strong>not</strong> tied to display.</p>
+++<p><strong>Payload:</strong> surface, count, <code>source: disk</code>, timestamp, optional <code>lastSuccessfulUpdateAt</code>.</p>
+++<p><strong>Pros:</strong> Clean separation; does not affect display/dismiss/interact counts.<br/><strong>Cons:</strong> New schema; needs Product/analytics pipeline approval.</p>
+++
+++<h4>Option 2 — Metadata on existing display event (not recommended v1)</h4>
+++<p><strong>Where:</strong> Add XDM field on <code>display</code> track, e.g. <code>meta.propositionSource: "disk"</code>.</p>
+++<p><strong>Pros:</strong> Reuses existing pipeline.<br/><strong>Cons:</strong> Display count blends disk + network; reporting changes; offline display may never reach Edge anyway.</p>
+++
+++<h4>Option 3 — On dismiss/interact only (weak)</h4>
+++<p><strong>Cons:</strong> Misses cards shown but never interacted with; same reporting pollution as Option 2.</p>
+++
+++<h4>Option 4 — App-level analytics only (no SDK change)</h4>
+++<p>Integrator fires their own event when <code>update</code> fails and <code>get</code> succeeds offline.</p>
+++<p><strong>Pros:</strong> Zero SDK schema work.<br/><strong>Cons:</strong> Inconsistent across customers; Assurance/debug still needed for Adobe support.</p>
+++
+++<ac:structured-macro ac:name="info" ac:schema-version="1" ac:macro-id="analytics-rec-001"><ac:rich-text-body><p><strong>Recommendation:</strong></p>
+++<ul>
+++<li><strong>Campaign metrics (display/dismiss/interact):</strong> Keep unchanged — user actions only.</li>
+++<li><strong>Operational / offline observability:</strong> New <code>proposition.cache.served</code> event (or Assurance-only v1, analytics v1.1).</li>
+++<li><strong>Assurance (debug):</strong> §6.6 Option D — can ship without Edge analytics initially.</li>
+++</ul></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
+++
+++<h3>6.8 Timeout, low network vs offline (OQ-1)</h3>
+++<p>The <strong>200ms</strong> and <strong>5s</strong> numbers measure different things. Use this framing with Product:</p>
+++
+++<table class="wrapped"><tbody>
+++<tr><th>State</th><th>What device sees</th><th>SDK behavior</th><th>Typical latency</th></tr>
+++<tr><td><strong>Offline</strong></td><td>No path (airplane mode, no interface)</td><td>Can skip Edge immediately via path monitor; disk hydrate &lt;200ms</td><td><strong>Sub-second</strong> if queue not blocked</td></tr>
+++<tr><td><strong>Low / degraded network</strong></td><td>Path &quot;satisfied&quot; but Edge slow or failing</td><td>Still tries Edge; waits for retries/timeouts</td><td><strong>3–10+ seconds</strong></td></tr>
+++<tr><td><strong>Online</strong></td><td>Healthy path + Edge responds</td><td>Normal fetch + persist</td><td>Network RTT dependent</td></tr>
+++</tbody></table>
+++
+++<ac:structured-macro ac:name="note" ac:schema-version="1" ac:macro-id="timeout-key-001"><ac:rich-text-body><p><strong>Key point:</strong> <strong>200ms is the disk-read budget, not a network timeout.</strong> Disk hydrate is fast. The <strong>5 second</strong> pain is the <strong>Event Hub callback timeout</strong> while <code>getPropositions</code> waits behind a queued <code>updatePropositions</code> or behind a slow/failing Edge call — not disk I/O.</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
+++
+++<h4>What fixes what</h4>
+++<table class="wrapped"><tbody>
+++<tr><th>Problem</th><th>Fix</th><th>Target latency</th></tr>
+++<tr><td>True offline, empty UI for 5s</td><td>Network gate on update + <strong>cache-first get</strong> + bypass <code>eventsQueue</code> for reads</td><td>&lt;200ms–1s</td></tr>
+++<tr><td>Low network, user waits for Edge</td><td><strong>Not solvable with 200ms timeout</strong> — network genuinely slow</td><td>3–10s unless we fail fast</td></tr>
+++<tr><td>Integrator chains update → get offline</td><td>Document <strong>get-first pattern</strong>; skip update when offline</td><td>Sub-second</td></tr>
+++</tbody></table>
+++
+++<h4>Should we expose configurable timeout from authoring (like Optimize)?</h4>
+++<p><strong>Short answer:</strong> <strong>Not for disk serve.</strong> Optional <strong>fail-fast network timeout</strong> for update — different knob.</p>
+++<table class="wrapped"><tbody>
+++<tr><th>Knob</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Sensible default</th><th>Authoring UI?</th></tr>
+++<tr><td><strong>Read callback timeout</strong></td><td>Max wait for <code>getPropositions</code> response</td><td>5s (or 10s if disk path)</td><td>SDK constant; rarely app-config</td></tr>
+++<tr><td><strong>Update / Edge fail-fast timeout</strong></td><td>Stop waiting on degraded network</td><td>3–5s configurable</td><td>Maybe Launch/app config — <strong>not</strong> per card</td></tr>
+++<tr><td><strong>Disk hydrate</strong></td><td>Load from persistence</td><td>N/A — always fast</td><td>No timeout needed</td></tr>
+++</tbody></table>
+++
+++<p><strong>Why not 200ms authoring timeout for &quot;low network&quot;:</strong></p>
+++<ul>
+++<li>200ms is below typical Edge RTT on poor Wi‑Fi (Disney parks use case).</li>
+++<li>A 200ms update timeout would <strong>always</strong> fall back to disk on degraded networks — even when fresh content would arrive in 2–3s.</li>
+++<li>That creates a product tradeoff: <strong>stale cache fast</strong> vs <strong>fresh content slow</strong> — PM must choose explicitly, not via a universal 200ms.</li>
+++</ul>
+++
+++<ac:structured-macro ac:name="info" ac:schema-version="1" ac:macro-id="pm-language-001"><ac:rich-text-body><p><strong>Suggested PM language:</strong></p>
+++<p>Offline vs low network are different problems. When the device has <strong>no network</strong>, we can detect that locally (path monitor) and serve cached content cards in <strong>under 200ms</strong> from disk — provided the app reads cache first and we do not block reads behind a network update.</p>
+++<p><strong>Low network</strong> (connected but slow) is not offline. Edge may still take <strong>3–5 seconds or longer</strong>. A 200ms timeout would force cache fallback on almost every degraded session, meaning users would often see <strong>stale</strong> content instead of waiting for fresh campaigns.</p>
+++<p>The current <strong>5 second</strong> timeout is the <strong>API callback limit</strong> while the SDK waits for Messaging to respond — often because a network update is queued ahead of the read, not because disk is slow.</p>
+++<p><strong>Proposal:</strong></p>
+++<ol>
+++<li><strong>Offline:</strong> network availability check → skip Edge update → serve disk immediately (target sub-second).</li>
+++<li><strong>Low network:</strong> keep configurable <strong>update</strong> timeout (e.g. 3–5s fail-fast) at app/Launch level — not per message in authoring.</li>
+++<li><strong>Do not</strong> use 200ms as a universal network timeout; reserve 200ms as the <strong>disk hydrate performance target</strong> only.</li>
+++</ol></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
+++
+++<h4>Product decision matrix</h4>
+++<table class="wrapped"><tbody>
+++<tr><th>PM priority</th><th>Behavior</th></tr>
+++<tr><td><strong>Show something immediately</strong></td><td>Cache-first get + offline gate; optional short update timeout (2–3s) then refresh</td></tr>
+++<tr><td><strong>Freshness over speed</strong></td><td>Longer update timeout (5–10s); accept wait on low network</td></tr>
+++<tr><td><strong>Hybrid (recommended)</strong></td><td>Show disk immediately (cache-first); background update with 5s timeout; refresh UI if network succeeds</td></tr>
+++</tbody></table>
+++
+++<h4>OQ-5 / OQ-1 summary</h4>
+++<table class="wrapped"><tbody>
+++<tr><th>Question</th><th>Suggested answer</th></tr>
+++<tr><td>Assurance when serving from disk?</td><td><strong>On read completion</strong> — event with <code>propositionSource: disk</code> + network status; plus <strong>on update skip</strong> when offline</td></tr>
+++<tr><td>Analytics when serving from disk?</td><td><strong>Separate operational event</strong> — not on display/dismiss/interact v1</td></tr>
+++<tr><td>200ms timeout?</td><td><strong>Disk target only</strong> — not network; low network needs 3–5s+ or fail-fast policy at app level</td></tr>
+++<tr><td>Authoring timeout like Optimize?</td><td><strong>Launch/app config for update fail-fast</strong> — not per-card authoring</td></tr>
+++</tbody></table>
